1
00:04:56,842 --> 00:05:02,842
Did you ever hear the words "Blue Sunshine"? Try to
remember...your life may depend on it.

2
00:09:53,684 --> 00:09:59,684
Blue Sunshine is a science fiction, horror, mystery
film directed by Jeff Lieberman.

3
00:14:50,526 --> 00:14:56,526
At a party, someone goes insane and murders three women.

4
00:19:47,368 --> 00:19:53,368
Falsely accused of the brutal killings, Jerry is on the run.

5
00:24:44,210 --> 00:24:50,210
More bizarre homicides continue with alarming frequency all over town.

6
00:29:41,052 --> 00:29:47,052
Trying to clear his name, Jerry discovers the shocking truth...people are losing their hair and turning into
violent psychopaths and the connection may be some LSD all the murderers took a decade before.

7
00:34:37,894 --> 00:34:43,894
Jerry Zipkin, played by Zalman King.

8
00:39:34,736 --> 00:39:40,736
Alicia Sweeney, played by Deborah Winters.

9
00:44:31,578 --> 00:44:37,578
Edward Flemming, played by Mark Goddard.

10
00:49:28,421 --> 00:49:34,421
David Blume, played by Robert Walden.

11
00:54:25,263 --> 00:54:31,263
Detective Clay, played by Charles Siebert.

12
00:59:22,105 --> 00:59:28,105
Wendy Flemming, played by Ann Cooper.

13
01:04:18,947 --> 01:04:24,947
Blue Sunshine is a 1977 American horror film written and directed by Jeff
Lieberman, and starring Zalman King, Deborah Winters, and Mark Goddard.

14
01:09:15,789 --> 01:09:21,789
The plot focuses on a series of random murders in Los Angeles, in which the only common link between
the perpetrators is a mysterious batch of LSD that they had all taken years prior.

15
01:14:12,631 --> 01:14:18,631
Over the years, the film attracted a cult following, and was released on
special edition DVD by Synapse Entertainment in 2003.

16
01:19:09,473 --> 01:19:15,473
It has been shown at many film festivals since.

17
01:24:06,315 --> 01:24:12,315
The film explores themes of lsd, drug use, epidemic, baldness.

18
01:29:03,157 --> 01:29:09,157
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
